From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:56:27 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 170/297] Meridian: no crash where Lens, reading mode and other
 Chromium features reach for Chrome's window

Lens's overlay (a user's crash: OverlayBaseController::ShowOverlay CHECKed
contents_web_view) closes its session instead when the window has no
contents view for it, whichever entry point opened it (page, PDF, picture,
video frame). Also guarded where Meridian's WebUI window has no BrowserView or
toolbar: the sad tab, reading mode's immersive view (it stays in the side
panel), the media remoting dialog, Cut/Copy/Paste actions (the page's own),
the page-action callbacks, the file access and memory saver bubbles, the idle
bubble, tab search's lookup, the Journeys side panel and Indigo's overlay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
